                <div id="tab11" class="content active">

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30 active" data-rel="tab-a-1">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> What is the focus of the PGP in UI/UX & AI Product Design at Masters’ Union?
                                </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer active" id="tab-a-1">The PGP in UI/UX & AI Product Design focuses on building
                            end-to-end design capability, covering user research, problem framing, UX strategy,
                            interaction design, visual design, and design systems. The programme emphasises real-world
                            problem solving, design thinking, and collaboration with product and engineering, preparing
                            students to design meaningful, scalable digital experiences.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-2">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> Who should apply to this programme?
                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-2">This programme is for anyone looking to start or transition
                            into a career in UI/UX and Product Design. It is suitable for fresh graduates, early-career
                            professionals, and career switchers who aspire to work as Product Designers, UI/UX
                            Designers, UX Researchers, Strategists, or in emerging roles such as Conversational UX,
                            AR/VR Design, Accessibility Design, and Prompt Design for product interfaces.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-3">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What skills will I gain by the end of the programme?
                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-3">Graduates develop strong capabilities in user research, UX
                            design, UI design, prototyping, usability testing, design systems, and stakeholder
                            communication. In addition, the program builds critical thinking, design leadership, and
                            collaboration skills required to work effectively in fast-paced product teams.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-4">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> What career opportunities are available after completing this
                                programme?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-4">After completing the programme, students can pursue roles such
                            as Product Designer, UI/UX Designer, Interaction Designer, UX Researcher, or Design
                            Consultant. Graduates are well-positioned to work with startups, tech companies,
                            enterprises, design agencies, or even build and scale their own products.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-5">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Does the programme offer industry exposure or hands-on experience?
                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-5">Yes. The programme is built to take you from Designer to a
                            Product Builder and a Global Operator through a multi-track, studio-led curriculum that
                            mirrors how real product organizations work. Students design, prototype, and iterate inside
                            simulated product teams, working on real-world problems under the guidance of top design
                            leaders. You graduate with proof, not promises–a portfolio that shows clear evidence of your
                            thinking, building, and shipping.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-6">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> How is this programme different from traditional design courses?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-6">Unlike traditional design courses that focus mainly on tools
                            or aesthetics, this programme takes a product-first approach. It combines design craft with
                            business context, user empathy, and product strategy, ensuring graduates understand not just
                            how to design, but why design decisions matter in building successful products.</p>
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div id="tab33" class="content">

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-c-1">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> If an applicant doesn’t have an undergraduate degree, can they still
                                apply?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-c-1">Yes. An undergraduate degree is not
                            mandatory for admission to the PGP in UI/UX & AI Product Design. While many participants may
                            hold undergraduate or advanced degrees, we also welcome applicants with strong professional
                            experience, a proven track record of learning, and clear motivation to build a career in
                            design. Applicants completing their undergraduate degree by May of the following year are
                            also eligible to apply.

                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-c-2">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Is there an age limit for admission?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-c-2">There is no strict age limit for the
                            programme. Eligibility is evaluated holistically based on your experience, intent, and
                            readiness for the programme. Applicants with more than 10 years of work experience are
                            encouraged to connect with the admissions team at <a class="link-red"
                                href="mailto:pgadmissions@mastersunion.org"
                                target="_blank">pgadmissions@mastersunion.org</a> for personalised guidance on programme
                            fit. </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-c-3">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> Will not having a design background affect my chances of admission?
                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-c-3">Yes. A prior design background is
                            preferred but actively encourages applications from diverse academic and professional
                            backgrounds, including engineering, business, marketing, psychology, arts, and more. </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-c-4">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What kind of candidates is the programme looking for?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-c-4">We are looking for individuals who are
                            curious, self-driven, and eager to build. Strong candidates show openness to feedback,
                            comfort with ambiguity, empathy for users, and the ability to learn by doing. Leadership
                            potential, initiative, and a growth mindset are key indicators of success in the programme.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-c-5">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Is there a minimum GPA requirement?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-c-5">TNo, there is no minimum GPA requirement.
                            Since grading systems vary globally, admissions decisions are not based solely on GPA. We
                            consider your academic journey holistically, looking at coursework, learning outcomes, and
                            overall performance, alongside professional experience and motivation.
                        </p>
                    </div>

