                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-e-1">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Can I submit non-design or cross-disciplinary work?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-e-1">No, we need a design and product portfolio
                            that shows user-centric thinking, problem solving, or are equally valid.

                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-e-2">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What kind of work should be included in the portfolio?
                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-e-2">Your portfolio should highlight how you
                            think, not just what you designed. This can include user research, problem framing,
                            wireframes, UI explorations, prototypes, experiments, or shipped work. We value clarity of
                            thought, decision-making, and iteration more than polish alone.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-e-3">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What format should the portfolio or submission be in?
